Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Filter the device list by compliance

Administrators want to find the devices that break their policies without
opening each one.

The device list gets a compliance filter next to the platform filter, with
the choices all, compliant and non-compliant. The device service already
knew each device's compliance state; the list now asks for it.
---
Expected: worth documenting. Triage picks _devices.md, perhaps also _devices_id.md. The draft adds the compliance filter to the paragraph about filters on _devices.md; if _devices_id.md was picked, it comes back no-change.

 public/app/devices/devices.controller.js | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/public/app/devices/devices.controller.js b/public/app/devices/devices.controller.js
index a604f07..31e64dd 100644
--- a/public/app/devices/devices.controller.js
+++ b/public/app/devices/devices.controller.js
@@ -1,6 +1,6 @@
 angular.module('mobivisor').controller('DevicesCtrl', ['$scope', 'deviceService', function ($scope, deviceService) {
   $scope.devices = [];
-  $scope.filter = { platform: 'all', enrolled: true };
+  $scope.filter = { platform: 'all', enrolled: true, compliance: 'all' };
 
   $scope.reload = function () {
     deviceService.list($scope.filter).then(function (devices) {
